  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nA + B = ₹9000\n\n(4/11) × A = (3/5) × B\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nTo solve, use the equation derived from the given ratios.\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n(4/11) × A = (3/5) × B\n\n⇒ B = (4/11) × A ÷ (3/5)\n\n⇒ B = (4 × 5) ÷ (11 × 3) × A\n\n⇒ B = (20/33) × A\n\nWe know A + B = ₹9000\n\n⇒ A + (20/33) × A = ₹9000\n\n⇒ A × (1 + 20/33) = ₹9000\n\n⇒ A × (33/33 + 20/33) = ₹9000\n\n⇒ A × (53/33) = ₹9000\n\n⇒ A = ₹9000 × (33/53)\n\n⇒ A = ₹5603.8\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (1).**\n\n8c:Tc10,\n<span s",
